  "label": "Hillary Clinton is mapped as having more skeletons in her closet than Jeffrey Dahmer",
  "description": "The text 'has more skeletons in her closet than jeffrey dahmer' is directly mapped onto Hillary Clinton, who is visually depicted in the image. The mapping implies that Hillary Clinton is the entity possessing the 'skeletons in her closet' — i.e., hidden secrets or crimes — and that the quantity or severity of these is being compared to the extreme criminality of Jeffrey Dahmer. This is an analogical mapping where the textual accusation is projected onto the visual subject, creating a grotesque and inflammatory comparison.",
